    },
    "text": "mf asking to write down rules I didn’t write smh 😔 im p sure this is the first time I’ve written that rule, conjured from self reflection at your bidding! If anyone broke your game it was you by not taking the next turn ;) \n\nI think yall‘ll be better served by threading these replies, or stuffing them together in a manner most concatenous. No character limit over here so loquacity  not a problem.\n\nSpeaking of gears, do you have the tech to post pics of design? I know the engine will generate svg drawings, but that’s not as satisfying as like an iso view snip. Just good fodder for socmed, yall can show off :)\n\nYou also finished up in a hurry to reply. It’s good! It’s ok to do that. But if I were you I would strike while the iron is hot, use part of the turn to move your own projects forward or research new ones. We of course need fresh fodder for the engine to work \n\nPossibly a good first target or series of targets is social graph analytics on delvetown. It’s a pretty small network, I bet you could easily make a force directed graph of all users with emergent clustering already. It could probably be entirely frontend too. Maybe start with a node (me for example) and spider out through the network"
   },
