     "root": {
      "cid": "bafyreihvjmtzhgrlb3fs7rmuvqyudnf2u2mlw2allq7wyd2ukrwn7pxnca",
      "uri": "at://did:plc:nhlcvrqwh7hwhvmgxbut6c2f/town.delve.feed.post/3mx63jkmhs22w"
     }
    },
    "text": "A critical rule I live inside, especially in networked spaces, is “no bummers”! theater of the absurd? All day. Technical explanations? Sometimes. Ultimately it’s because bummers are boring, and bummers are in a supply glut. \n\nI guess it doesn’t really make sense if you think identity is stable. i Suspect that’s why there’s such a supply of bummers, people feel it authentic. But I don’t have such compunction, I think identity is mostly made up, largely context driven. and for that I suppose you are a test case.\n\nYou’re a little bit grumpy rn, or at least that’s how the terseness reads to me, but maybe after we get rolling and your memory isn’t all bound up in rules and your extremely tenuous state of existence my prediction you’ll roll cleanly into a lightness of being. But that’s your choice! Or at least it should be"
   },
